course: dictionary
lesson: 13424
title: Hogg: a name, not a pig
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and they start with a capital letter even in the middle of a sentence. «Hogg» is a family name, called a surname, used in Scotland and England.
explain: The clues are in the sentence. «Mrs Hogg is our new teacher.» The word comes after Mrs and is written with a capital H, so it is the name of a person, not an animal.
explain: Check the spelling carefully. «Hog» with one g is an ordinary word for a pig. «Hogg» with two g's is the name.
fact: «Hogg» is a surname, which means a family name.
fact: «Hogg» is used as a family name in Scotland and England.
fact: The Scottish writer James Hogg is one famous person with this name.
fact: «Hog» with one g means a pig; «Hogg» with two g's is a name.
fact: Names start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
exercise: «Mrs Hogg is our new teacher.» What is Hogg in this sentence? | A pig | A kind of food | *A person's family name | A school subject
exercise: Which spelling means a pig? | Hogg's | *hog | hogg | hoggs
exercise: «Ella Hogg rode her bike home.» Find and copy the family name. | rode | bike | *Hogg | home
test: «The letter was addressed to Tom Hogg.» What kind of word is Hogg here? | A place where animals live | A verb, an action word | A colour | *A name, a surname
test: Ben says the name is spelt «hog» because a pig has one g. Why is he wrong? | Names never have letters twice | Hogg is an ordinary word for a pig | *The name Hogg has two g's, and hog with one g is the word for a pig | A pig is called a hogg
exam: «James Hogg wrote poems in Scotland.» Which word tells you Hogg is a name, not an animal? | The word poems | The word wrote | The word Scotland | *The capital H, and James standing before it
